post-it: Computer doesn't start - just a bunch of text
symptoms:
	Non-System disk error at startup
		category: At startup
	Floppy in drive A:
checks:
	Boots from C:
		shows: it stops at "Non-System disk or disk error"
software steps:
	Eject the floppy from drive A:
	Press a key, or restart, with no floppy in A:
notes:
	Error message when booting "Non-System disk or disk error
	Replace and press any key when ready"
	In the game, the drive's eject button sticks out and pulses while a diskette is in A:; a click ejects it (Mascolls, #204).
